um.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T13:51:34-07:00","id":933567,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://We&#39;ve had similar conversations before.\" target=\"_blank\">We've had similar conversations before.</a> I'd love more Demon, but even I have to admit the line is in great shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T13:58:33-07:00","id":933572,"title":"","content":"At the very least, I wouldn't be surprised if we saw a Dark Eras 2 with new Demon stuff in it. And the upcoming Dark Eras Companion has a new Demon setting in it already!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T18:42:15-07:00","id":933680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/932595-will-there-be-anymore-books?p=932940#post932940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What more could you be wanting? As someone else said, what you are asking for sounds like flowers of hell. Or do you just want more for the sake of more?</div> </div> </div> </div>Night Horrors: Demon is the one that's bandied about the the most often. (Hell, it's the one I bandy around the most) The STG gave a complete tool box for assembling angles and other threats, but most story tellers won't turn their nose up at pre-made antagonists, especially give the sheer amount of imagination that's been put into the Night Horrors books. Just about every line has a Night horrors book, and a few have a dedicated antagonist source book (Autumn Nightmares for changeling, a bunch from Mage and Hunter)<br /> <br /> Cryptids: Another great idea that gets minimal coverage beyond the tool box. Cryptids give the GMC a different feel than the standard CoD, less Supernatural, more X-files. Additionally, crypto-flora has only barely been touched on, despite hints that there are enough different species to fill a botanical garden.<br /> <br /> There were plenty, plenty more suggested in a earlier thread, but I think those two are the most likely candidates as they already have precedent in other lines and they avoid being more of the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 08-02-2016, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T18:44:14-07:00","id":933681,"title":"","content":"I think it basically comes down to whether or not the writers think that there is an area of the fluff or rules that could use expansion. And as it stands, I'm not sure there is. Maybe Rose and Co. will eventually think otherwise, but basically, Demon is in pretty good shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T19:07:04-07:00","id":933693,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mind seeing a book on Stigmatics, cultists, and general ground-level weirdness; maybe toss in a robust Cryptid creation chapter as well.","signa